(349, 'Do you watch Anime?', '<p>Anime is a form of entertainment that combines animated storytelling, hand-drawn visuals and music. The concept of anime originated in Japan and has become popular worldwide. The popularity of anime continues to grow as more <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/people\" target=\"_blank\">people</a> become aware of its existence. However, many people are unaware of the historical context in which anime originated. Therefore, they may view anime as a subgenre of Japanese pop culture that isn\'t worth studying. They may also view it as a waste of time since there are so many other forms of entertainment available. However, anime is a form of entertainment that can be easily studied since it\'s available in many forms.</p><p>Anime is a form of entertainment that combines animated storytelling, hand-drawn visuals and music. This form of entertainment is made up of a large variety of anime shows that are broadcast on television, online and on mobile phones. There are many different genres of anime that focus on different stories and characters. The large variety of anime makes it easy for fans to discover new series that interest them. When someone is interested enough in a genre of anime to become knowledgeable about it\'s proof that the genre is worth studying.</p><p>Also, they watch anime for the story-driven content. The stories in anime are often set in fantasy or science fiction settings where characters undergo fantastical events. Some stories focus on romance or <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/relationships\" target=\"_blank\">relationships</a> between characters. The stories in these genres are often easy to follow and can be interesting to a non-fan audience member.</p><p>On the other hand, some anime fans watch anime for the action and adventure. Action anime typically focuses on stories where characters face dangerous situations and must use their skills to survive them. Adventure anime typically focuses on stories where characters travel to new locations and meet new people. Many anime fans feel that both story types are worth watching since they cater to different interests.</p><p>Although some fans watch anime for the story-driven content, others watch it for educational purposes. Many fans watch anime so they can learn Japanese vocabulary and learn about different cultures from around the world. Watching anime can also be a good way to learn about history if the show takes place in a historical setting.</p><p>Although some people may view anime as substandard or inferior to other forms of entertainment, it is still a worthwhile form of entertainment to study. Anime can be easily watched on television or online or downloaded onto a mobile phone for convenience\'s sake. It is still worthwhile to study because it has such a large following worldwide and can teach fans new vocabulary words they may not have encountered before. It\'s up to the viewer\'s discretion whether or not they want to spend time studying this genre; however, they should at least consider it when they have free time during the week.</p><p><strong>So, we wanted to know your answer for theme in poll&nbsp;Do you watch Anime?. Take part in this survey and discussion.</strong></p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-01-20 12:03:49', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1642680229, NULL),
(350, 'Do you Think that NFT is a Scam?', '<h2>Do you think that nft is a scam? Poll</h2><p>However, NFT scams are common because they are easy to create and only exist online. In fact, according to a survey conducted by PrivacyHQ, 90% of <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/NFT\" target=\"_blank\">NFT</a> owners have experienced NFT scams. The same survey found that half of the respondents did not have access to their NFTs at some point.</p><p>NFT scams and bubbles are everywhere these days. Don\'t be surprised - you should be careful. In the end, NFTs are about ownership transparency and authenticity. So how do these bubbles and scams happen and what can you do to avoid them?</p><h2>What are your thoughts on the potential of nft?</h2><p>The NFT market is huge and growing. While the possibilities for NFTs may seem endless, as with any new asset/asset class, you should invest with caution due to the extremely risky and speculative nature of new, undefined markets.</p><p>NFTs are at a critical moment in consumer awareness. The technology has a lot to offer, but the bursting of the NFT value bubble has led many to see it as nothing more than a waste of capital. Now is the perfect time for entertainment companies to launch NFTs that offer practical rather than speculative investment options and change public perception forever.</p><p>Various NFTs have sold millions of dollars so far. As blockchain technology expands, some predict it will become an important part of the future of digital assets. In order to take advantage of the potential boom, it is imperative to know everything about NFTs. And your opinoin in poll&nbsp;Do you think that nft is a scam?</p><h2>What are your thoughts on the potential of blockchain technology?</h2><p>It\'s worth noting that the views expressed in the survey were not always negative -- at least as far as the underlying technology is concerned. The survey found that 41 percent of IT professionals are positive about the potential of blockchain technology to benefit <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/Humanity\" target=\"_blank\">humanity</a>, for example by securing transactions in areas ranging from healthcare to contracts.</p><p>Currently, blockchain technology is not very powerful. There are many inefficiencies and deficiencies. Are there scams and scams? A lot, of course, because you have a new value distribution system. When it comes to money, there are always scams and scams.</p><p>But because blockchain opens up new possibilities for governance, there is a lot of experimentation. I think it\'s a R&amp;D expense in a new area, not the totality and end result of how a Web 3 organization should be structured. Many of them will fail. But something new will emerge from it.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>So we want you to vote your opinoin on poll&nbsp;Do you think that nft is a scam? But not only vote but also share your experience in comments.&nbsp;Because we want to see full picture of what people thinking on it.</strong></p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-01-24 12:45:22', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1643028322, NULL),
(351, 'Are you Satisfied With your Current Job?', '<p>Job dissatisfaction is a common problem that affects millions of <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/people\" target=\"_blank\">people</a> worldwide. It\'s a natural feeling when you\'re unhappy with the conditions or your current job. However, you can learn to be satisfied with your current job by finding ways to make it a better fit for you. When you\'re satisfied with your current job, you\'ll derive the maximum benefit from it.</p><h2>Survey Are you Satisfied with your Current Job? Some arguments for yes and no.</h2><p>Many people feel dissatisfied with their current jobs because they don\'t like the conditions or the tasks. Other people may feel dissatisfied with their current jobs because of a bad fit for their skills and interests. Regardless of the reason, finding ways to better your situation is essential for your well-being. For example, you can negotiate for more pay or better working conditions to make your job more appealing. You can also look for jobs that better match your interests and skills so you\'ll have more free time to do what you love. Whatever you do, finding ways to better your situation is essential to being satisfied with your current job.</p><p>Sometimes people feel dissatisfied with their current jobs because they don\'t like the tasks or the conditions. For example, a person may hate their current job because they do menial tasks all day long. In addition, they may dislike the conditions because they are always hot and sweaty. Regardless of the reason, finding ways to better your situation is essential for your well-being. For example, you can negotiate for more pay or better working conditions to make your job more appealing. You can also look for jobs that better match your interests and skills so you\'ll have more free time to do what you love. Whatever you do, finding ways to better your situation is essential to being satisfied with your current job.</p><p>Not everyone is happy with their current jobs because they don\'t like the conditions or the tasks. Some people are discontent with their current jobs because they don\'t feel challenged enough. They may also feel dissatisfied because they are bored out of their minds at their current jobs. Regardless of the reason, finding ways to better your situation is essential for your well-being. For example, you can negotiate for more pay or better working conditions to make your job more appealing. You can also look for jobs that better match your interests and skills so you\'ll have more free time to do what you love. Whatever you do, finding ways to better your situation is essential to being satisfied with your current job.</p><p>Regardless of the reason why someone is not satisfied with their current job, finding ways to better it is essential for overall happiness at <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/work\" target=\"_blank\">work</a>. Finding ways to better your current situation should be a top priority when looking for a new job because it will make a world of difference in how you feel about yourself and your job. Finding ways to better yourself at work can be difficult and time consuming, but it is essential to being satisfied at work and in life overall.</p><p><strong>So, we wanted to know your answer for theme in poll&nbsp;Are you Satisfied With your Current Job?&nbsp;Take part in this survey and discussion.</strong></p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-01-26 10:17:57', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1643192277, NULL),
(352, 'Are You Vaccinated?', '<p>In a large multi-national survey, 71.5% would likely get vaccinated and 61.4% would comply if employers suggested doing so.In the <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/USA\" target=\"_blank\">USA</a>, 65% believed parents should be required to vaccinate ; but the rate of refusal grew from 24% to 42.2% in North Carolina and 16.4% to 35.4% in Maine, if it was mandated by the federal <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/government\" target=\"_blank\">government</a> [23. Views varied concerning <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/children\" target=\"_blank\">children</a>: 51% of Americans believed K-12 schools (kindergarten through grade 12) should require COVD-19 vaccines, while 75% of Texans thought the government should require child vaccination for infectious diseases [54. Parents may have different considerations for vaccinating their children than themselves. One survey reported 76.02% vs. 74.38% receptivity and another 45% vs. 36.2% [5; 58% would do so as soon as possible,though having chronic illness was a deterrence.Those who indicated refusal for themselves also would not vaccinate their children.</p><h2>Poll for theme Are You Vaccinated?</h2><p>\r\nThree international studies investigated healthcare professionals’ attitudes and found similar concerns about vaccine safety and effectiveness and receptivity predictors including previous vaccination history, perceived risk or exposure, and being older, male, or a doctor [7,55. Healthcare workers in Indonesia had greater acceptance than the public (OR: 1.57, 95% CI: 1.12–2.20) while nurses in Hong Kong indicated low intention (40%).Israeli doctors reported slightly higher self-acceptance (78% vs. 75%), but were less likely to vaccinate their children than the public (60% vs. 70%).</p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-01-26 10:25:32', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1643192732, NULL),
(353, 'Do you think America is not helping Ukraine enough?', '<h2>Overview of the current situation in Ukraine.</h2><p><!-- x-tinymce/html --><a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Russia\" target=\"_blank\">Russia</a>’s war against <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Ukraine\" target=\"_blank\">Ukraine</a> is causing a humanitarian, social and economic crisis for the Ukrainian <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/people\" target=\"_blank\">people</a>. The consequences of this full-scale military invasion are disrupting the global supply of commodities, sharply increasing food and energy prices, and treating the recovery from the <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Covid\" target=\"_blank\">COVID</a>-19 pandemic. Countries with established commercial and financial ties with the economies of Russia and Ukraine appear to be particularly vulnerable.Assessing the Impact of Russia’s <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/War\" target=\"_blank\">War</a> against Ukraine on Eastern Partner Countries investigates the exposure of Eastern Partner countries (Armenia, Azerbaijan, <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Georgia\" target=\"_blank\">Georgia</a>, Republic of Moldova and Ukraine) to the economic shocks caused by the war, and in particular through the impact that the conflict is having on inflation, migration, remittances, investment and trade.This report is published as part of the multi-country project “EU4Business: From Policies to Action – phase 2”, implemented in the Eastern Partnership with the financial support of the European Union within the EU4Business initiative[1].</p><p><!-- x-tinymce/html -->“One year into Russia’s invasion of Ukraine, the world continues to witness the horrific destruction inflicted on the country and its people. We will continue supporting the people of Ukraine through urgent repair projects and coordination with the <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/government\" target=\"_blank\">Government</a> for recovery and reconstruction efforts.” - World Bank Group President David Malpass.</p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-03-28 08:30:27', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1648456227, NULL),
(354, 'Do you consider the Russian army to be the second most powerful army in the world?', '<h2>Overview of the Russian army and its capabilities.</h2><p>The reformed and revitalized Russian <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/military\" target=\"_blank\">military</a> is increasingly powerful and proficient. However, <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Russia\" target=\"_blank\">Russia</a> remains suspended between the large but limited army of its past and the expensive but proficient professional military model. Does this mixed manpower system give Russia the best or the worst of both worlds?.</p><p><!-- x-tinymce/html -->In&nbsp;Understanding the Russian Military Today, a&nbsp;five-day, professional development program, participants explored all the elements of Russian military power: its composition and prospects, its social and historical foundations, its doctrine, and current operations. Through interactive seminars and hands-on simulation exercises,&nbsp;think tank analysts, academics, security specialists, and <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/government\" target=\"_blank\">government</a> officials came together to develop new interdisciplinary analyses and approaches. As a final exercise, participants were tasked with developing short, independent research papers that explored one of four major themes: Russian society, strategy, and history; elements of Russian military power; recent uses of Russian military power; and resources behind Russian military power. CSIS is pleased to present their work below. The papers are a testament to knowledge gained throughout the course, yet each stands on its own as knowledge added to a growing community of Russian military and security experts.</p><p><a></a></p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-04-09 08:10:19', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1649491819, NULL),
(355, 'Do you think that Chinas government doing right thing with lockdown?', '<h2>Overview of China\'s lockdown measures</h2><p><!-- x-tinymce/html -->China\'s government implemented strict lockdown measures in response to the <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Covid\" target=\"_blank\">COVID</a>-19 <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/pandemic\" target=\"_blank\">pandemic</a>. These measures included travel restrictions, mandatory quarantines, and the closure of businesses and public spaces. The government\'s quick and decisive action in implementing these measures helped to control the spread of the virus and prevent it from overwhelming the country\'s healthcare system. However, the strict restrictions and their enforcement have been a source of controversy and criticism. Despite this, the Chinese <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/government\" target=\"_blank\">government</a> has continued to defend their approach, arguing that it is necessary to protect the health and safety of the population.</p><p><!-- x-tinymce/html -->The strict enforcement of lockdown measures in <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/China\" target=\"_blank\">China</a> has been a key factor in their success in controlling the spread of the virus. The government has used a combination of technology and manpower to ensure that individuals are adhering to the restrictions. This includes using surveillance cameras, tracking mobile phones, and deploying thousands of officials to enforce the rules. While some have criticized the government\'s methods as invasive and authoritarian, others argue that they are necessary to prevent the spread of the virus and protect public health.</p><p><!-- x-tinymce/html -->The impact of China\'s lockdown measures on daily <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/life\" target=\"_blank\">life</a> and the economy has been significant. The restrictions have disrupted daily routines and forced businesses to close, leading to a sharp decline in economic activity. However, the government has implemented various measures to support individuals and businesses affected by the lockdowns, including providing financial assistance and subsidies. Despite the economic costs, many argue that the strict measures were necessary to prevent the spread of the virus and protect public health.</p><p>So,&nbsp;do you think that Chinas government doing right thing with lockdown? Answer in that poll and join the discussion in the comments</p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-04-11 09:57:17', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1649671037, NULL),
(356, 'Do you think that Finland need to join NATO?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html -->\r\n<h3>Arguments for Finland joining NATO</h3>\r\n<p>There are several compelling arguments for <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Finland\" target=\"_blank\">Finland</a> to join <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Nato\" target=\"_blank\">NATO</a>. One of the most significant benefits of NATO membership is increased security and protection from external threats. As NATO\'s Secretary-General Jens Stoltenberg stated recently, \"Joining NATO is good for Finland, it is good for Nordic security, and it is good for NATO as a whole\". Finland\'s historical policy of military non-alignment has left it vulnerable to external aggression, particularly from <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Russia\" target=\"_blank\">Russia</a>. However, by joining NATO, Finland would have access to the collective defense capabilities of the alliance, which would provide a strong deterrent against potential aggressors.</p>\r\n<p>Another advantage of Finland joining NATO is access to the military capabilities and resources of the alliance. Finland has a relatively small military, and joining NATO would provide access to a wider range of military equipment and technology. This would enable Finland to better defend itself against potential threats and enhance its military capabilities. Additionally, Finland\'s participation in NATO would allow for increased cooperation and coordination with other member countries in areas such as intelligence sharing, military training, and joint military exercises.</p>\r\n<p>Finally, joining NATO would strengthen Finland\'s ties with other member countries, particularly those in the Nordic region. Finland already participates in Nordic Defense Cooperation (NORDEFCO), a regional defense initiative that includes Norway, Sweden, Denmark, and Iceland. However, joining NATO would further enhance Finland\'s cooperation with these countries and provide a framework for greater collaboration on defense and security issues. Furthermore, Finnish and Swedish membership in NATO would bolster the alliance\'s collective defenses in northern <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/Europe\" target=\"_blank\">Europe</a> and its eastern flank, which is particularly important given the current security environment in Europe. Overall, joining NATO would provide significant benefits for Finland\'s security and defense, as well as strengthen its ties with other member countries.</p>\r\n<h3>Arguments against Finland joining NATO</h3>\r\n<p>One of the main arguments against Finland joining NATO is the preservation of its neutral position and independence. Finland has a long history of neutrality, dating back to the Cold <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/War\" target=\"_blank\">War</a>, and has maintained this stance even as its Nordic neighbors, Norway and Denmark, joined NATO. Joining NATO would mean abandoning this neutral position and aligning Finland with a military alliance, which could potentially compromise its independence and sovereignty. Some argue that Finland\'s current policy of military non-alignment has served it well and that joining NATO could potentially create more problems than it solves.</p>\r\n<p>Another argument against Finland joining NATO is the potential for provocation of Russia. Russia has historically been sensitive to NATO expansion and has previously threatened retaliation against countries that seek to join the alliance. Some experts argue that Finland joining NATO could escalate tensions with Russia and lead to increased military activity in the region. Furthermore, it could lead to a deterioration of relations between Finland and Russia, which could have economic and political consequences for both countries.</p>\r\n<p>Maintaining positive relations with non-NATO countries is also a concern for those opposed to Finland joining NATO. As a neutral country, Finland has been able to maintain positive relations with both NATO and non-NATO countries, such as Russia and <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/China\" target=\"_blank\">China</a>. Joining NATO could potentially strain these <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/tag/relationships\" target=\"_blank\">relationships</a> and limit Finland\'s ability to engage in diplomacy and cooperation with non-NATO countries. Additionally, it could lead to Finland being perceived as a partisan player in international affairs, rather than a neutral mediator.</p><p><a></a></p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 2, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-04-12 17:42:15', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1649785335, NULL),
