(362, 'Do you think that Elon Musk will change Twitter for the better?', '<h2>Some people think that elon musk will damage twitter for the worse.</h2><p>Now billionaire Musk is trying to pull out of the blockbuster deal, ruthlessly making Twitter look worse than when he said he would buy it. With every obnoxious tweet and public taunt, Musk has eroded trust in the social <a href=\"https://en.online-statistics.org/search/tag/media\" target=\"_blank\">media</a> company, shaken employee morale, spooked would-be advertisers, highlighted its financial woes, and spread the word Misinformation about how Twitter works.</p><p>\"We believe that the sheer nature of free speech on Twitter and Musk\'s preferences may lead to worse businesses and platforms promoting big brands, even if Musk can find a way to increase usage or users of the platform,\" Weiser wrote. road. in a blog post.</p><p>Musk has said he thinks Twitter should be \"<strong>more reluctant to take things down</strong>\" and be \"<strong>very cautious about a permanent ban.</strong>\" That could mean a long list of controversial far-right figures and conspiracy theorists alike will soon be back on the platform.</p><h2>Some people think that elon musk will improve twitter for the better.</h2><p>Could Musk make Twitter great again? At least that\'s what the right thinks. Conservatives cheered Musk\'s takeover. They seem to see billionaire purchases of social networks as a victory for free speech and a rebuke to Big Tech. (No one does mental gymnastics like conservatives.)</p><p>Like other Twitter users, Musk isn\'t shy about sharing his thoughts on issues that need fixing on the site and posting his candid remarks to his 95 million followers. (Measured by his followers, Musk has more influence on social media than Twitter CEO Parag Agrawal and Twitter co-founder Jack Dorsey combined.) The tweets offer a love-hate relationship with Twitter. Relationship Insights.</p><p><a></a>So we wanted to know your opinion about \"<strong>Do you think that Elon Musk will change Twitter for the better</strong>?\" take part in a poll and in the discussion below.</p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 2, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2022-04-27 12:16:47', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1651061807, NULL),
