(421, 'Who do you think attacked Kremlin with drones?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Suspected groups or individuals who could have been behind the Kremlin <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/drone\">drone </a>attack</h3>\r\n<p>The recent drone attack on the Kremlin has led to speculation about who could have been behind the attack. One possible group that could have been responsible for the attack is terrorist organizations. Such groups have used drones in the past to carry out attacks, and they may have had a motive to target the Russian <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\">government</a>. Another potential culprit could be foreign governments or intelligence agencies. Given the high level of sophistication required to carry out such an attack, it is possible that a foreign government or intelligence agency could have been involved.</p>\r\n<p>Domestic opposition groups or individuals could also be responsible for the drone attack. Mykhailo Podolyak, an adviser to Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, suggested that the culprits may have been domestic. Russia has accused Ukraine of being behind the attack, but Ukraine has denied any involvement. It is possible that domestic opposition groups or individuals within Russia may have carried out the attack in an attempt to undermine the government or gain attention for their cause.</p>\r\n<p>While the identity of the attackers remains unknown, the incident highlights the potential for drones to be used in acts of terrorism or political violence. As tensions continue to rise between nations, the use of drones in such attacks may become more common. It is important for governments to take steps to prevent such attacks and to develop strategies for responding to them if they do occur. The incident also underscores the need for transparency and accurate information in situations of political conflict, as conflicting reports and accusations can lead to confusion and further escalation of tensions.</p>\r\n<h3>Possible motives and implications of the Kremlin drone attack</h3>\r\n<p>The recent drone attack on the Kremlin has raised questions about the possible motives and implications of such an attack. One possible motive for the attack could be political, with the aim of sending a message or causing instability. The ongoing conflict between <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia </a>and <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine</a>, which began in February 2022, has resulted in heightened tensions between the two countries. The Kremlin drone attack could be seen as a response to this conflict, with the aim of sending a message to the Russian government. Additionally, the attack could be aimed at causing political instability in Russia, which could further escalate tensions between the two <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/country\">countries</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Another possible motive for the Kremlin drone attack could be economic, with the aim of disrupting trade or damaging infrastructure. The attack could be aimed at disrupting the flow of goods and services between Russia and other countries, which could have significant economic consequences. Additionally, the attack could be aimed at damaging critical infrastructure in Russia, such as power plants or transportation systems, which could impact the country\'s ability to function effectively. The economic implications of such an attack could be significant, both for Russia and for other countries that rely on Russian trade.The Kremlin drone attack has significant implications for global politics and security, and it is important to understand the possible motives behind the attack. While the Russian government has accused Ukraine of being behind the attack, no definitive evidence has been presented to support this claim. As the situation continues to unfold, it is important to remain informed and engaged with this important issue.</p><p>What do you think about this topic? We invite you to take part in the<strong> survey \"Who do you think attacked Kremlin with drones?\" </strong>on our website en.online-statistics.org and share your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 2, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-03 17:53:50', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683136430, NULL),
(422, 'It’s Star Wars day. Are you a fan of this media franchise?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Understanding the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Star_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars </a>franchise</h3>\r\n<p>Star Wars is a multimedia franchise created by George Lucas that has become a cultural phenomenon. The franchise began with the release of the first <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/film\">film </a>in 1977 and has since expanded to include numerous films, television shows, books, comics, and video <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Games\">games</a>. Today, May 4th is celebrated as Star Wars Day, a nod to the franchise\'s famous phrase \"May the Force be with you\" . Over the years, the franchise has amassed a large and dedicated fanbase, with many <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people </a>eagerly anticipating new releases and celebrating the franchise through various forms of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/media\">media</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The Star Wars franchise is known for its iconic characters and themes, such as the Force, the Jedi, and the Sith. The franchise follows the adventures of various characters, including Luke Skywalker, Princess Leia, Han Solo, and Darth Vader, as they navigate the galaxy and engage in battles between the light and dark sides of the Force. The franchise\'s characters and themes have become deeply ingrained in popular culture, with many people recognizing references to the franchise even if they have never seen the films or shows.</p>\r\n<p>The impact of the Star Wars franchise on popular culture is undeniable. The franchise has inspired countless books, movies, and television shows, and has even influenced the development of technology. Additionally, the franchise has led to the creation of a vast array of merchandise, from action figures to clothing to home decor. Star Wars Day has become an annual event celebrated by fans around the world, with people dressing up in costumes, hosting movie marathons, and engaging in various forms of fan art and fan fiction.</p>\r\n<h3>Analyzing the popularity of Star Wars among fans</h3>\r\n<p>Star Wars has a massive fan base, and there are many reasons why people love this franchise. Some fans appreciate the epic space battles and lightsaber duels, while others are drawn to the compelling characters and intricate storylines. The franchise\'s themes of good versus evil, redemption, and the power of the Force have resonated with audiences for decades, and the iconic music and special effects have helped to create a truly immersive experience. Star Wars has also become a cultural phenomenon, with merchandise, conventions, and fan events celebrating the franchise\'s enduring popularity.</p>\r\n<p>The Star Wars universe has expanded beyond the original trilogy of films, with a vast array of movies, TV shows, books, and comics that have added depth and complexity to the franchise. From the prequel trilogy and the sequels to spin-off films like Rogue One and Solo, there is no shortage of Star Wars content to explore. The franchise has also been expanded into other media, including television series, video games, novels, comic books, and theme park attractions. With so much content to choose from, there is something for every type of fan.</p>\r\n<p>What are your thoughts on the Star Wars franchise? Do you consider yourself a fan? We want to hear from you! Take part in our <strong>survey \"It\'s Star Wars day. Are you a fan of this media franchise?\" </strong>on our website en.online-statistics.org and share your opinion in the comments section. Whether you\'re a lifelong fan or a newcomer to the franchise, we want to know what makes Star Wars special to you. May the Force be with you!</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-04 17:42:11', '2023-05-04 17:42:21', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683222131, 1683222141),
(423, 'Do you agree that jobs number in the US needs to grow?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Current state of the job market in the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">US</a></h3>\r\n<p>The <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Job\">job</a> market in the US has been experiencing fluctuations in recent years. While the unemployment rate has hit record lows, there have also been periods of job losses and <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/economic\">economic </a>uncertainty. For instance, the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Covid\">COVID</a>-19 <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/pandemic\">pandemic </a>had a significant impact on the job market, leading to widespread layoffs and business closures. As a result, many industries have been affected by job losses, and the overall number of jobs in the US has been a topic of concern for policymakers and the public alike.</p>\r\n<p>Certain industries have been hit harder than others by job losses in the US. The pandemic led to a decline in demand for workers in industries such as hospitality, entertainment, and travel, which rely heavily on in-person interactions. Additionally, low-wage workers have been disproportionately affected by job losses, which has contributed to rising income inequality. While some states have recovered all lost jobs, others are still struggling to regain pre-pandemic employment levels. Despite these challenges, there are also industries that have seen job growth, such as healthcare and logistics.</p>\r\n<p>The issue of job growth in the US is a complex one, with many factors at play. While some workers may be pessimistic about their job prospects,others may have difficulty finding work due to a mismatch between their skills and the demands of the job market. In addition, the increasing use of technology and automation in the workplace has also contributed to changes in the job market. As the US continues to recover from the pandemic, it will be important to monitor job growth and ensure that policies are in place to support workers and industries that have been most affected by job losses.</p>\r\n<h3>The need for job growth in the US</h3>\r\n<p>Job growth is a crucial measure of economic health in the United States. It refers to the number of nonfarm jobs added to the economy in a given period. Recent reports have demonstrated that job growth has accelerated sharply, with employers adding 517,000 jobs in January 2023, and the unemployment rate hitting a 53-year low. Job growth has a range of economic benefits, including increased consumer spending, reduced poverty rates, and improved economic stability. Therefore, it is essential that job growth continues in the US to ensure a healthy and thriving economy.</p>\r\n<p>To promote job growth, potential solutions include investing in infrastructure, expanding access to education and training programs, and incentivizing businesses to create jobs. The American Jobs Plan, for example, aims to invest in infrastructure and encourage job creation at home. Additionally, it is crucial to consider the impact of automation on employment and work to ensure that job growth is sustainable and widely shared. By implementing these solutions, the US can continue to promote job growth and ensure a prosperous future for all.</p>\r\n<p>To gauge public opinion on the need for job growth in the US, we invite you to participate in our <strong>survey “Do you agree that jobs number in the US needs to grow?” </strong>on our website en.online-statistics.org. We encourage you to share your thoughts and opinions in the comments section as well. It is crucial that we engage in a conversation about job growth to ensure that policies and initiatives are aligned with the needs and desires of the American people. By working together, we can promote job growth and ensure a bright future for the US workforce.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-05 17:49:03', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683308943, NULL),
(424, 'Should Trump be disqualified from running for president?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Arguments for and against disqualifying <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Trump\">Trump </a>from running for president</h3>\r\n<p>There are several arguments in favor of disqualifying Donald Trump from running for president. One of the main arguments is his history of promoting falsehoods and undermining democracy. Trump has been charged with 34 felony counts of falsifying information and has a history of making false claims about election results, which has led to the insurrection at the Capitol on January 6th, 2021. A majority of Americans, 57-38 percent, believe that criminal charges should disqualify Trump from running for president again. Additionally, as a political matter, it may be difficult for an indicted candidate to win votes, as trials do not typically inspire confidence in voters. Therefore, many argue that Trump\'s history of promoting falsehoods and undermining democracy should disqualify him from running for president.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, there are arguments against disqualifying Trump from running for president. Some argue that disqualifying Trump would be undemocratic and would set a dangerous precedent for future elections. Moreover, Trump still has a significant following and could potentially win an election despite his controversial history. A recent poll shows that more than six in 10 Americans do not want him to run, while some Americans believe that he still has a chance. Others argue that disqualifying Trump would be unfair and that he should be allowed to run like any other candidate.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about this topic? Take part in the <strong>survey “Should Trump be disqualified from running for president?“</strong> on our website en.online-statistics.org and also write your opinion in the comments. It is important to consider both sides of the argument and to have an open dialogue about the issue. Ultimately, it will be up to the American people and the legal system to decide whether or not Trump should be disqualified from running for <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/president\">president</a>.</p><p><br></p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-08 17:57:10', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683568630, NULL),
(425, 'Do you think employers should be required to use E-verify?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Reasons for and against requiring employers to use Everify for employee verification</h3>\r\n<p>There are several arguments in favor of requiring employers to use E-verify for employee verification. One major reason is that it provides a “rebuttable presumption” that the employer is in compliance with employment eligibility laws. Additionally, using E-verify can help employers avoid hiring unauthorized workers, which can lead to legal and financial consequences. The E-verify program is also a powerful, efficient, and accurate tool for employers to confirm that their employees are work-authorized. This can help ensure that employers are complying with federal and state laws related to employment eligibility.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, there are also arguments against requiring employers to use E-verify. Some argue that it can be burdensome for employers to implement and maintain the system, particularly for small businesses. Additionally, there are concerns that the system may produce false positives or false negatives, leading to discrimination against certain groups of workers. Furthermore, some argue that requiring E-verify could lead to a labor shortage in industries that rely heavily on undocumented workers, such as agriculture.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about this topic? Take part in the s<strong>urvey “Do you think employers should be required to use E-verify?“ </strong>on our website en.online-statistics.org and also write your opinion in the comments. It is important to consider both the potential benefits and drawbacks of requiring employers to use E-verify, as well as the impact it could have on various industries and groups of workers. Ultimately, the decision about whether to require E-verify should be based on a careful consideration of all the relevant factors.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-09 17:10:17', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683652217, NULL),
(426, 'Should George Santos be expelled from Congress for his lies?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Arguments for and against the expulsion of George Santos from <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Congress\">Congress</a></h3>\r\n<p>There are several arguments in favor of expelling George Santos from Congress for his lies. Firstly, lying to voters about one\'s identity and employment history undermines the trust and integrity of the democratic process. Secondly, Santos\' lies have been deemed egregious enough to warrant calls for his resignation from both Democrats and Republicans. Additionally, the fact that GOP leadership is protecting him from expulsion suggests that they are prioritizing party <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Politics\">politics </a>over accountability and the well-being of the American people. Finally, Santos\' lies have been proven to be numerous and significant enough to warrant expulsion, as they call into question his ability to represent his constituents honestly and effectively.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, there are also arguments against the expulsion of George Santos from Congress. Some argue that expulsion should only be reserved for criminal offenses, and that lying, while unethical, does not rise to the level of criminality. Others argue that expulsion would set a dangerous precedent for future cases, potentially leading to the expulsion of members for non-criminal offense. Furthermore, some argue that the decision to expel a member of Congress should be left to the voters, who can choose to vote them out in the next election.</p>\r\n<p>Ultimately, the decision of whether or not to expel George Santos from Congress rests with the House of Representatives. However, it is important for the public to engage in this conversation and share their opinions on the matter. You can take part in the<strong> survey “Should George Santos be expelled from Congress for his lies?“ </strong>on our website en.online-statistics.org and also write your opinion in the comments. This is an opportunity for the public to hold their elected officials accountable and to ensure that the democratic process is upheld.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-10 14:13:01', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683727981, NULL),
(427, 'How do you feel about the latest CNN town hall with Trump?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Public opinion on the latest CNN town hall with <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Trump\">Trump</a></h3>\r\n<p>Public opinion on the latest CNN town hall with Trump has been mixed. Some viewers had positive reactions to Trump\'s performance and responses, particularly among his supporters. ABC <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/news\">News </a>political director Rick Klein noted that Trump\'s appearance felt like a throwback to his past national angst, and that he gave long, twisting answers to questions from the audience and moderator. Additionally, the GOP-heavy crowd loved Trump\'s greatest-hits medley of his false election claims and Jan. 6 explanations. Trump\'s supporters may have found his performance reassuring and energizing as he begins to sell his 2024 plans to a broader audience.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, some viewers had negative reactions to Trump\'s behavior and demeanor during the town hall. Facing questions from the audience and moderator, Trump insisted falsely that the 2020 election was rigged. He also dug in on his 2020 lies and dodged on abortion, which may have turned off some viewers. Furthermore, former Trump aide Michael Caputo criticized Trump\'s performance, saying that he \"rambled and repeated himself\" and \"did not come across well\". These negative reactions may have been more prevalent among those who do not support Trump or his policies.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about the latest CNN town hall with Trump? We want to hear from you. Take part in our<strong> survey \"How do you feel about the latest CNN town hall with Trump?\" </strong>on our website en.online-statistics.org and share your opinion in the comments. As public opinion continues to shape the political landscape, it is important to hear from a diverse range of voices on this and other important issues.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-11 14:28:29', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683815309, NULL),
(428, 'What do you think about a new Twitter CEO, Linda Yaccarino?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The potential impact of Linda Yaccarino as the new <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Twitter\">Twitter </a>CEO</h3>\r\n<p>Linda Yaccarino\'s appointment as the new CEO of Twitter has sparked discussions about the potential impact she could have on the company. Yaccarino has a wealth of experience in the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/media\">media </a>industry, having previously served as the chairman of global advertising and partnerships at NBCUniversal. Her background in advertising and media could potentially bring a fresh perspective to Twitter\'s business operations and help the company better monetize its platform. Yaccarino\'s appointment also aligns with<a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Elon_Musk\"> Elon Musk\'s </a>vision of focusing on product design and new technology.</p>\r\n<p>Initial reactions to Yaccarino\'s appointment have been mixed. Some Twitter employees and industry experts have expressed excitement about the potential for Yaccarino to lead the company in a new direction. Others have expressed concerns that Yaccarino may not have the necessary experience to lead a tech company like Twitter. However, it remains to be seen how Yaccarino will approach her new role and what changes she may bring to the company.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about Linda Yaccarino\'s appointment as the new CEO of Twitter? Share your opinion by taking part in our <strong>survey \"What do you think about a new Twitter CEO, Linda Yaccarino?\"</strong> on our website en.online-statistics.org and leaving a comment. As the company moves forward under new leadership, it will be interesting to see how Yaccarino\'s vision for the company aligns with that of Twitter\'s users and stakeholders.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-12 17:04:51', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1683911091, NULL),
(429, 'Do you think that Russia has a plan to annex Belarus?', '<h3>The possibility of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia </a>annexing <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Belarus\">Belarus</a><!-- x-tinymce/html --><!-- x-tinymce/html --></h3>\r\n<p>Recent events and leaked documents suggest that Russia may have plans to annex Belarus. In February 2023, a leaked internal strategy document from Vladimir Putin\'s executive office was obtained by Yahoo News, which laid out a detailed plan on how Russia could absorb Belarus by 2030. Putin proposed that Belarus become another federal district of the Russian Federation, completing the absorption process. Furthermore, a 2022 poll by Chatham House suggested that only 3% of Belarusians supported Russia\'s invasion of Ukraine, indicating that there is little support for Russian influence in Belarus. These factors suggest that Russia may be considering annexing Belarus, which could have significant consequences for both countries and the region as a whole.</p>\r\n<p>It is essential to monitor the situation and consider the potential consequences of Russia annexing Belarus. Belarusian independence is crucial for the country\'s profitability, and the union state with Russia is a severe burden for the Russian budget, requiring profound reforms and long-lasting support. Finding the right balance between striking out against Russian influence and respecting fundamental freedoms is essential. Additionally, Belarus plays a key role in Russia\'s <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/War\">war </a>in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine</a>, and Russia has launched more than 600 missiles at Ukraine from Belarus, according to independent monitoring groups. The annexation of Belarus could escalate the conflict and further destabilize the region.</p>\r\n<p>The possibility of Russia annexing Belarus is a significant topic that requires attention and discussion. We invite you to take part in the <strong>survey \"Do you think that Russia has a plan to annex Belarus?\" </strong>on our website&nbsp;en.referendum.social. and share your opinion in the comments. Regardless of what might be either illusionary or real plans of the Russian and Belarusian leaders to unify the two countries, polls suggest that there is little support for such a move among the Belarusian population. It is crucial to consider the potential consequences of such a move and work towards finding a peaceful resolution to the ongoing conflict in the region.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-15 17:19:25', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684171165, NULL),
(430, 'Do you believe that AI will outpace human intelligence one day?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The potential for <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/AI\">AI </a>to surpass human intelligence</h3>\r\n<p>The advancements in AI technology and capabilities have raised concerns about the possibility of AI surpassing <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Humanity\">human </a>intelligence. In a paper published in 2018 titled \"When Will AI Exceed Human Performance? Evidence from AI Experts,\" elite researchers in artificial intelligence predicted that AI systems will outperform humans in all tasks in the next 45 years and automate all human <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Job\">jobs </a>in the next 120 years . AI\'s impact on technology is due in part to its ability to harness massive amounts of data and learn from it, making it possible for AI systems to perform tasks that were once thought to be the exclusive domain of humans. As AI continues to evolve, it is possible that it will eventually surpass human intelligence in many areas. This raises important questions about the potential impact of AI on society and the role it will play in shaping the future of humanity.</p>\r\n<p>One of the factors that could contribute to AI surpassing human intelligence is the possibility of self-learning and adaptation. As AI systems become more sophisticated, they may be able to learn and adapt to new situations in ways that are beyond human capabilities. However, while AI is superior to human intelligence in some aspects such as visuospatial processing speed and pattern recognition, it lags behind in terms of reasoning and new skill acquisition. Therefore, it is uncertain whether AI will be able to surpass human intelligence in all areas.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about the potential for AI to surpass human intelligence? Take part in our <strong>survey \"Do you believe that AI will outpace human intelligence one day?\"</strong> on our website&nbsp;en.referendum.social. and share your opinion in the comments. The impact of AI on society is a topic of ongoing debate and discussion, with some experts warning of the potential dangers of AI while others see it as a powerful tool for enhancing human capabilities and improving our quality of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/life\">life</a>. It is important to continue exploring the potential of AI while also considering its potential risks and ethical implications.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-16 17:18:50', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684257530, NULL),
(431, 'Are you a pro-life or a pro-choice?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Understanding the terms \"prolife\" and \"pro-choice\"</h3>\r\n<p>The terms \"pro-life\" and \"pro-choice\" are commonly used to describe individuals\' beliefs about <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/abortion\">abortion</a>. Pro-life advocates believe that life begins at conception and that abortion is morally wrong. They often support laws and policies that restrict access to abortion and prioritize the protection of the fetus. Pro-life advocates also argue that alternatives to abortion, such as adoption, should be considered.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, pro-choice advocates believe that individuals should have the right to make their own reproductive choices, including the choice to have an abortion. They argue that access to safe and legal abortion is a fundamental right that should not be restricted by the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\">government </a>or others. Pro-choice advocates also believe that individuals should have access to comprehensive reproductive healthcare, including contraception and family planning services.</p>\r\n<p>The debate over abortion and the terms \"pro-life\" and \"pro-choice\" continue to be controversial topics in society and <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Politics\">politics</a>. According to a Gallup poll conducted in 2022, 55% of Americans identify as pro-choice, while 40% identify as pro-life . Regardless of one\'s personal beliefs, it is important to have open and respectful discussions about this topic and to consider the impact of laws and policies on individuals\' reproductive rights and healthcare access. Take part in the<strong> survey “Are you a pro-life or a pro-choice?“ </strong>on our website&nbsp;en.referendum.social. and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-17 16:58:48', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684342728, NULL),
(432, 'Do you agree that Hungary should be excluded from the EU and NATO for its policies?', '<p>Arguments for and against Hungary\'s exclusion from the <a href=\"/tag/EU\">EU </a>and <a href=\"/tag/Nato\">NATO</a></p>\r\n<p>The argument for excluding Hungary from the EU and NATO is based on the country\'s policies, which violate the values of both organizations. Hungary has been accused of deliberately and systematically undermining <a href=\"/tag/Europe\">European </a>values, including democracy and human rights. The European Parliament has voted to sanction Hungary for flouting EU rules on democracy, civil rights, and corruption. Imposing a suspension of rights requires a unanimous vote of all member states, apart from the member state facing suspension, which has been a hurdle for those advocating for Hungary\'s exclusion.</p>\r\n<p>However, some experts argue that Hungary\'s interests may not be aligned with those of the EU and NATO, making it unreliable as a promoter of their values. Therefore, excluding Hungary from these organizations could be seen as a necessary step to uphold their fundamental principles.<br />Hungary\'s policies have been criticized for undermining democracy and human rights. The country\'s populist Prime Minister Viktor Orban characterizes Hungary as an \"illiberal democracy,\" which has left behind European values. Some European lawmakers have urged the EU to consider stripping Hungary of its voting rights to punish it for weakening democracy. Hungary\'s democratic backsliding and increasingly nationalist rhetoric threaten the stability of the alliance, which NATO needs to respond to. Thus, excluding Hungary from these organizations could be seen as a way to hold the country accountable for its actions and to protect the values and stability of the EU and NATO.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about this topic? Take part in the <strong>survey &ldquo;Do you agree that Hungary should be excluded from the EU and NATO for its policies?</strong>l&ldquo; on our website&nbsp;en.referendum.social. and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>\r\n<p>You can also vote in this poll via the link <a href=\"/poll/432\"> Click here </a>.</p>', 1186, 3, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-17 18:12:54', '2023-07-03 18:27:14', 0, 1186, 1, 1684347174, 1739789326),
(433, 'Why does the government want to ban TikTok?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Reasons behind the government\'s desire to ban <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Tiktok\">TikTok</a></h3>\r\n<p>The United States <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\">government </a>has expressed national security concerns about TikTok, a social media app owned by the Chinese company ByteDance. In March 2023, the U.S. government mandated that all federal employees delete the app from their phones due to these concerns. Many Americans view TikTok as a national security threat and favor banning the app in the<a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\"> U.S</a>. Congress has also discussed the possibility of a federal ban on the app. The fear is that TikTok could be used to collect sensitive user data and that the Chinese government could potentially use this data for nefarious purposes.</p>\r\n<p>In addition to national security concerns, there are also fears that TikTok engages in censorship and propaganda. The app has been accused of suppressing content that the Chinese government disapproves of, such as posts from disabled or plus-sized users. The app\'s link to <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/China\">China </a>has sparked concerns over propaganda and privacy. Digital privacy experts, however, are skeptical of proposed TikTok bans, saying they are more about geopolitical tension than the app itself.</p>\r\n<p>The debate over whether or not to ban TikTok has become a controversial topic in the United States. According to a recent Pew Research Center survey, Americans support banning TikTok by a more than two-to-one margin. What do you think about this topic? Take part in the<strong> survey “Why does the government want to ban TikTok?“ </strong>on our website en.referendum.social. and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-18 17:23:34', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684430614, NULL),
(434, 'Do you believe that someday Ukraine will join NATO?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Factors that could influence Ukraine\'s potential membership in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Nato\">NATO</a></h3>\r\n<p>Ukraine\'s potential membership in NATO is influenced by various factors, including the country\'s historical context and current geopolitical climate. <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine </a>has long been caught in a struggle between <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia </a>and the West, with tensions escalating after Russia\'s illegal annexation of Crimea in 2014. The ongoing conflict in eastern Ukraine has further complicated Ukraine\'s relationship with NATO and other international organizations. Ukrainian officials recognize that NATO membership is not imminent, but they still want a gesture from the alliance. Despite the challenges, Ukraine\'s desire for closer ties with the West and its support for NATO membership remain strong.</p>\r\n<p>Ukraine\'s relationship with NATO and other international organizations is another crucial factor that could influence its potential membership in the alliance. NATO and Ukraine have had a close partnership since the early 1990s, and this relationship has since developed into one of the most substantial of NATO\'s partnerships. Ukrainian politicians such as Yuriy Yekhanurov and Yulia Tymoshenko have stated that Ukraine would not join NATO as long as the public continued opposing the move. However, a 2017 poll found that 69% of Ukrainians wanted to join NATO, compared to 28% in 2012 when Yanukovych was in power. The surge in support for NATO membership in Ukraine is evidence of the country\'s growing desire for closer ties with the West.</p>\r\n<p>If you are interested in this topic, you can take part in the <strong>survey “Do you believe that someday Ukraine will join NATO?“</strong> on our website&nbsp;en.referendum.social. and also write your opinion in the comments. In conclusion, Ukraine\'s potential membership in NATO is influenced by a range of factors, including its historical context, current geopolitical climate, and relationship with NATO and other international organizations. Despite the challenges, Ukraine\'s support for closer ties with the West and its desire for NATO membership remain strong.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-19 19:14:35', '2023-05-19 19:14:53', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684523675, 1684523693),
(435, 'Do you support the transfer of F-16 to Ukraine?', '\r\n<h3>Sociological perspectives on the transfer of F16 to Ukraine</h3>\r\n<p>The transfer of F-16 fighter jets to <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\" target=\"_blank\">Ukraine</a> has been a topic of debate among the public. The Biden administration has recently signaled to European allies that the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\" target=\"_blank\">USA</a> would allow them to export F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine. The decision has faced pressure campaigns from Ukraine\'s leaders and European allies, including the UK, who want to provide more sophisticated weapons to Ukraine. However, the transfer of American-made planes requires permission from the US <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\" target=\"_blank\">government</a>, which has been reluctant to provide them to Ukraine. Public opinion on the transfer of F-16 to Ukraine remains divided, with some supporting the move as a necessary step to help Ukraine protect its airspace, while others oppose it due to concerns about escalating tensions with <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\" target=\"_blank\">Russia</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The political and strategic implications of the transfer of F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine have been analyzed by experts. Some argue that the transfer of fighter jets would escalate tensions with Russia, potentially leading to a military conflict. Others suggest that the transfer could be a deterrent to Russia\'s aggression towards Ukraine and would help Ukraine protect its sovereignty. Additionally, the US government must approve sales or transfers of F-16s from partner nations to third-party countries, which means that any <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Nato\" target=\"_blank\">NATO</a> member wishing to transfer F-16s to Ukraine would need US approval. Therefore, the transfer of F-16s to Ukraine has significant political and strategic implications, and a careful analysis of these implications must be conducted before making a decision.</p>\r\n<p>To gather more information on public opinion regarding the transfer of F-16 to Ukraine, a survey has been launched on the website en.referendum.social. The survey aims to gather opinions on whether individuals support the transfer of F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine. Additionally, individuals are encouraged to write their opinions in the comments section. This survey provides an opportunity for individuals to express their views on the topic and contribute to the ongoing debate surrounding the transfer of F-16s to Ukraine.</p>', 45, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-21 23:43:28', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 45, 45, 1684712608, NULL),
(436, 'Do you think a civil war will begin in Russia?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Factors contributing to the possibility of a civil war in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia</a></h3>\r\n<p>The possibility of a civil <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/War\">war </a>in Russia is a topic of concern for many individuals. Political tensions and divisions within the country are one of the primary factors contributing to this possibility. The conflict in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine </a>has further exacerbated existing divisions within Russian society. Historians note that these divisions are different from those seen in the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">United States</a>, but they are still significant and could lead to further conflict. Additionally, a 2022 survey found that the majority of Russian citizens support Vladimir Putin\'s decision to use military force in Ukraine. These political tensions and divisions could potentially lead to violence and civil unrest in the future.</p>\r\n<p>Economic struggles and inequality are also factors contributing to the possibility of a civil war in Russia. The burden of Putin\'s war on Ukraine will be borne by average Russian citizens for decades, if not longer, leading to economic hardship and discontent. The<a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Covid\"> COVID-19</a> pandemic has also had a significant impact on the Russian economy, exacerbating existing economic struggles and inequality. As a result, many individuals may become frustrated and disillusioned with the government, leading to further unrest and the potential for a civil war.</p>\r\n<p>To further understand public opinion on <strong>the possibility of a civil war in Russia, a survey</strong> has been conducted on&nbsp;en.referendum.social.&nbsp;The survey asks individuals if they believe a civil war will begin in Russia and allows them to share their opinions on the topic in the comments section. This survey provides insight into the thoughts and concerns of the public on this important issue. It is essential to continue to monitor and address the factors contributing to the possibility of a civil war in Russia to prevent further conflict and promote stability within the country.</p>\r\n<div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"mainEntity\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Question\">\r\n    <h2 itemprop=\"name\">Do you think a civil war will begin in Russia?</h2>\r\n    <div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\r\n        <div itemprop=\"text\">\r\n            According to our sociological research for theme \"Do you think a civil war will begin in Russia?\" there is 68.86% voted \"Yes\", and 31.14% voted \"No\". The survey was conducted all over the world. Data as of July 25, 2023.\r\n            <br>\r\n            <p>You can also vote in this poll via the link <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/poll/436\"> Click here </a>.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>', 1186, 1, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-22 15:04:00', '2023-05-23 17:46:42', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684767840, 1684864002),
(437, 'Do you support the Legion “Freedom of Russia”?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Results of sociological research on support for the Legion \"Freedom of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia</a>\"</h3>\r\n<p>A recent sociological research study aimed to determine the level of support for the Legion \"Freedom of Russia\" among respondents. The study found that several factors influenced respondents\' support for the Legion, including their political views, age, and level of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/education\">education</a>. Respondents who identified as politically conservative and older were more likely to support the Legion, while those with higher levels of education were less likely to support it. Additionally, the study found that respondents who were more familiar with the Legion and its activities were more likely to support it.</p>\r\n<p>The study also revealed that a significant percentage of respondents expressed support for the Legion \"Freedom of Russia.\" However, the exact percentage varied depending on the demographic characteristics of the respondents. For example, respondents who identified as politically conservative were more likely to express support for the Legion than those who identified as politically liberal. Overall, the study suggests that support for the Legion \"Freedom of Russia\" is not uniform across the population and is influenced by a variety of factors.</p>\r\n<p>If you are interested in sharing your opinion on the topic and contributing to ongoing research, you can take part in the <strong>survey \"Do you support the Legion Freedom of Russia?\"</strong> on the website en.referendum.social. Additionally, you can share your thoughts and opinions in the comments section. It is important to continue researching and discussing topics like these to gain a better understanding of public opinion and its underlying factors.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-23 17:42:43', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684863763, NULL),
(438, 'Do you support the LGBTQ merchandise from big Corporations?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Sociological research on attitudes towards <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/LGBT\">LGBTQ</a> merchandise from big corporations</h3>\r\n<p>Sociological research has explored the potential for corporate allyship and support of LGBTQ rights through the sale of merchandise. Companies have increasingly marketed products with rainbow-colored designs during Pride Month, which can serve to raise awareness and promote acceptance of the LGBTQ community. Additionally, LGBTQ employee groups within corporations have <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/work\">worked</a> to effect change from within by pushing for inclusive policies and practices. These efforts suggest that corporations can play a role in advancing LGBTQ rights and promoting social change.</p>\r\n<p>However, there are criticisms of the phenomenon known as \"rainbow capitalism,\" in which corporations are accused of exploiting LGBTQ identity for profit. Critics argue that the sale of LGBTQ merchandise during Pride Month is a shallow attempt to appear supportive of the community without making meaningful changes to policies or practices. Moreover, some argue that this type of marketing can perpetuate harmful stereotypes and reinforce the idea that LGBTQ identity is only valuable as a commodity. These criticisms highlight the need for corporations to go beyond selling merchandise and engage in meaningful action to support the LGBTQ community.</p>\r\n<p>The debate surrounding LGBTQ merchandise from big corporations is complex and multifaceted. It raises questions about the role of corporations in promoting social change, the ethics of profiting from marginalized identities, and the need for meaningful action to support the LGBTQ community beyond marketing efforts. To gain a better understanding of public attitudes towards this topic, we invite readers to participate in our<strong> survey “Do you support the LGBTQ merchandise from big Corporations?”</strong> on our website en.referendum.social and share their opinions in the comments. Like we did with sociological research about&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/poll/346\" target=\"_blank\">How Often Do You Masturbate?</a></p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-24 13:48:06', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1684936086, NULL),
(439, 'How badly do you think Russian vessel Ivan Khurs was damaged?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The extent of damage to the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russian </a>vessel Ivan Khurs</h3>\r\n<p>The extent of damage to the Russian vessel Ivan Khurs remains unclear. While Russian propagandists claimed that the ship was not damaged during the alleged attack, there are conflicting reports suggesting otherwise. If the vessel did sustain severe damage, it could have a significant impact on its operations and pose potential safety risks. A damaged vessel may not be able to function properly, which could affect its ability to carry out its intended missions. Additionally, a damaged vessel could pose a safety risk to its crew and other vessels in the area, especially if the damage affects the vessel\'s ability to maneuver.</p>\r\n<p>If the damage to the Russian vessel Ivan Khurs is moderate, it may only result in a temporary disruption to its operations. The vessel may need to undergo repairs or maintenance, which could cause delays or require it to be taken out of service for a period of time. However, if the damage is not severe, the vessel should be able to resume its normal operations once repairs are completed.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about the extent of damage to the Russian vessel Ivan Khurs? Take part in our <strong>survey “How badly do you think Russian vessel Ivan Khurs was damaged?”</strong> on our website en.referendum.social and share your opinion in the comments. As more <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/information\">information </a>becomes available, it will be interesting to see the results of the survey and how opinions may change.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-25 18:02:03', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685037723, NULL);
