(440, 'Do you think that Ukraine should be allowed to strike Russian territory with F16s?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html -->\r\n\r\n<h3>The debate on whether <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine </a>should be allowed to strike Russian territory with F16s</h3>\r\n<p>The recent approval of European allies providing American-made F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine has sparked a heated debate on whether Ukraine should be allowed to strike Russian territory with these jets. Those in favor of Ukraine\'s right to strike argue that it is necessary for Ukraine to defend itself against Russian aggression. With Russian missiles and artillery regularly targeting Ukrainian civilians and infrastructure, Ukraine requires modern jets to strengthen its air and missile defenses, save lives, and protect civilians. Furthermore, retired generals have suggested that cross-border raids in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia </a>could be effective in deterring further Russian aggression .</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, those against Ukraine\'s right to strike argue that it could escalate the conflict and lead to further loss of life. Senior Russian diplomats have warned that the transfer of F-16 jets to Ukraine would raise the question of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Nato\">NATO\'s </a>role in the conflict and could provoke a military response from Russia . Additionally, some experts have suggested that Russian forces could easily impede Ukrainian F-16s from flying by targeting a few key airfields.</p>\r\n<p>Ultimately, the decision on whether Ukraine should be allowed to strike Russian territory with F-16s is a complex and contentious issue. It is important to consider the potential consequences and weigh the benefits against the risks. What do you think about this topic? Take part in the<strong> survey “Do you think that Ukraine should be allowed to strike Russian territory with F16s?“ </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-26 16:46:35', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685119595, NULL),
(441, 'Should medical use of Cannabis be legalized all over the world?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The argument for legalizing medical cannabis worldwide</h3>\r\n<p>There is a growing body of evidence supporting the medical benefits of cannabis, making a strong argument for its legalization worldwide. Proponents of medical cannabis argue that it can be effective in treating a variety of medical conditions, particularly when symptoms are difficult to manage with conventional pharmaceuticals. A 2022 committee report published by the National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Medicine\">Medicine </a>found significant evidence supporting the use of cannabis for certain medical conditions, including chronic pain and chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting. With 85% of Americans supporting the legalization of medical marijuana, it is clear that there is a strong public desire for access to this alternative treatment option.</p>\r\n<p>In addition to the medical benefits, legalizing medical cannabis could also have significant economic benefits for the pharmaceutical industry. A 2015 study found that support for medical cannabis legalization was associated with beliefs that it is a safe and effective treatment option, indicating a potential market for cannabis-based pharmaceuticals. Furthermore, as more states in the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">USA </a>have legalized marijuana, there has been a noticeable increase in the use of cannabis as an alternative to conventional pharmaceutical drugs. This suggests that the pharmaceutical industry could benefit from the legalization of medical cannabis, both in terms of developing new treatments and competing with the cannabis industry.</p>\r\n<p>The debate over legalizing medical cannabis is ongoing, with arguments on both sides. However, with nearly half of US states legalizing recreational marijuana and a growing number of countries legalizing medical cannabis, it is clear that there is a shift in public opinion towards acceptance of cannabis use. The potential benefits of legalizing medical cannabis, such as improved access to alternative treatment options and potential economic benefits, cannot be ignored. To share your opinion on this topic, take part in our<strong> survey \"Should medical use of Cannabis be legalized all over the world?\" </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-29 18:03:58', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685383438, NULL),
(442, 'Who do you think attacked Moscow with drones?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Possible suspects behind the Moscow drone attack</h3>\r\n<p>The recent drone attack on Moscow has raised questions about who could be responsible for such an attack. State actors with advanced drone technology are one possible suspect. Countries such as the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">USA</a>, <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/China\">China</a>, and Israel have developed sophisticated drone technology and have used it in various military operations. However, it is important to note that the attack on Moscow appears to have been carried out using commercial drones, which are widely available and accessible to individuals or small groups.</p>\r\n<p>Another possible suspect behind the drone attack on Moscow is individuals or small groups with access to commercial drones. Commercial drones are widely available and can be purchased easily online. These drones can be modified to carry small payloads, making them a potential threat in the hands of individuals or small groups with malicious intentions. The use of commercial drones in the attack on Moscow suggests that the perpetrators may not have had access to advanced <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/military\">military</a>-grade drones.</p>\r\n<p>What are your thoughts on this topic? Who do you think is behind the drone attack on Moscow? Take part in our survey on “Who do you think attacked Moscow with drones?” on our website en.referendum.social and share your opinion in the comments. It is important to gather a range of perspectives and opinions to better understand the potential motives and suspects behind the attack.</p>\r\n<div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"mainEntity\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Question\">\r\n    <h2 itemprop=\"name\">Who do you think attacked Moscow with drones?</h2>\r\n    <div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\r\n        <div itemprop=\"text\">\r\n            According to our sociological research for theme \"Who do you think attacked Moscow with drones?\" there is 60% voted \"False flag\", 16% voted \"Ukraine\", and 25% for \"Partisans\" . The survey was conducted all over the world. Data of update as  September 18, 2023.\r\n            <br>\r\n            <p>You can also vote in this poll via the link <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/poll/442\"> Click here </a>.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-30 18:04:44', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685469884, NULL),
(443, 'Do you think feminism is still relevant in today&#039;s society?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The relevance of feminism in today\'s <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/society\">society</a></h3>\r\n<p>To understand the relevance of feminism in today\'s society, it\'s important to consider its historical context. Feminism has been a movement for<a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Gender_equality\"> gender equality</a> that has been ongoing for over a century. While significant progress has been made in terms of women\'s rights, there are still ongoing issues of gender inequality that need to be addressed. Feminism today is the belief in the equality of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people </a>of all genders, aimed at dismantling gender inequality and the structures that support it. Despite the progress, there is still a need for continued efforts to ensure that gender equality is achieved in all areas of society.</p>\r\n<p>One of the ongoing issues of gender inequality is the gender pay gap, where <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Woman\">women </a>continue to earn less than <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/man\">men </a>for doing the same <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/work\">work</a>. Women also face barriers in accessing leadership positions and face discrimination in various aspects of their lives. A new global analysis of progress on gender equality and women\'s rights shows women and girls remain disproportionately affected by the ongoing <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/pandemic\">pandemic</a>. While some may argue that feminism is no longer relevant in today\'s society, the reality is that there are still significant barriers to achieving gender equality.</p>\r\n<p>The topic of feminism and its relevance in today\'s society is a complex one, and there are varying opinions on the matter. A national survey conducted in 2016 found that while a majority of Americans believe in the empowering and inclusive nature of feminism, there are still those who view it as polarizing. The public has mixed views on what feminism looks like today, with fewer than half of women saying the feminist movement has advanced gender equality. Take part in the<strong> survey “Do you think feminism is still relevant in today\'s society?“ </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-05-31 15:21:42', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685546502, NULL),
(444, 'Do you celebrate Pride Month?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The Importance of Celebrating Pride Month</h3>\r\n<p>Celebrating Pride Month is an important way to promote equality and acceptance for the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/LGBT\">LGBTQ</a>+ community. Pride events and celebrations provide a space for <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people </a>to come together and celebrate their identities, while also raising awareness and visibility for the community. During Pride Month, individuals and organizations alike can show their support for the LGBTQ+ community by participating in events, sharing resources, and educating themselves and others on issues affecting the community. Pride Month is also an opportunity to celebrate the progress that has been made towards equality and to reaffirm support for acceptance and understanding.</p>\r\n<p>Celebrating Pride Month can also help to raise awareness and visibility for the LGBTQ+ community, which is essential for promoting understanding and acceptance. Pride events and celebrations provide a platform for individuals to share their stories and experiences, helping to break down stereotypes and promote empathy and compassion. Additionally, Pride Month provides an opportunity to educate oneself and others on the challenges faced by the LGBTQ+ community and to advocate for change. By participating in Pride Month events and celebrations, individuals can show their support for the community and help to promote a more inclusive and accepting society.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about celebrating Pride Month? We want to hear your opinion! Take part in our <strong>survey “Do you celebrate Pride Month?” </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and share your thoughts in the comments. Celebrating Pride Month is an important way to show support for the LGBTQ+ community and promote equality and acceptance. By coming together to celebrate diversity and raise awareness, we can work towards a more inclusive and accepting society for all. So, join us in honoring LGBTQ+ pioneers who fought for equality through art, culture, civic action, community service, and more.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-01 19:56:06', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685649366, NULL),
(445, 'Do you believe the Russian-Ukrainian war could lead to a World War 3?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The potential impact of the Russian-Ukrainian conflict on global stability</h3>\r\n<p>The Russian-Ukrainian conflict has been ongoing since 2014, with tensions continuing to escalate in recent years. The conflict has the potential to escalate into a direct confrontation between <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia </a>and the West, which could have significant global implications. As Russia continues to escalate its nuclear threats, the world is on edge, with fears about the potential for World War III growing. The conflict has already had significant repercussions, including the displacement of civilians and loss of <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/life\">life</a>. The current situation and tensions suggest that the conflict could have a significant impact on global stability.</p>\r\n<p>Historical precedents suggest that regional conflicts have the potential to lead to global wars. The First and Second World <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/War\">Wars </a>both began as regional conflicts before escalating into global conflicts. While the current situation may not necessarily lead to a global war, it is important to consider the potential implications of the conflict on global stability. Some experts view the Russian-Ukrainian conflict as a manifestation of renewed geopolitical rivalry between major world powers, which could have significant global implications. It is important to closely monitor the situation and take steps to prevent the escalation of the conflict.</p>\r\n<p>The potential impact of the Russian-Ukrainian conflict on global stability is a topic of significant concern. We invite you to take part in our<strong> survey on the topic “Do you believe the Russian-Ukrainian war could lead to a World War 3?“</strong> on our website en.referendum.social and share your opinion in the comments. According to a 2022 poll of American public opinion on <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">U.S</a>. foreign policy by the Chicago Council on Global Affairs, 81% of Americans say the conflict in Ukraine is important to U.S. interests. The conflict has the potential to change NATO and the EU and transform thinking about global security. Western governments backing Kyiv in the Russo-Ukrainian war must wrestle with four persistent questions: what is the risk Russia poses to <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine</a>, to <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Nato\">NATO</a>, to the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/EU\">EU</a>, and to the global order?. It is essential to closely monitor the situation and take steps to prevent the escalation of the conflict.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-02 17:32:19', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685727139, NULL),
(446, 'Are you planning to vote in the next presidential election?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Reasons why voting in the presidential election is important</h3>\r\n<p>Voting in the presidential election is not only a right but also a civic responsibility of every eligible citizen. The foundation of American democracy is built on the right to vote, and free and fair elections that reflect the will of the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people </a>must be protected. By actively participating in democracy, citizens can exercise their voice and influence the direction of their country. Voting is a way for individuals to have a say in the policies and decisions that affect their lives, and it is an important way to hold elected officials accountable. Therefore, it is crucial for every eligible citizen to exercise their right to vote in the upcoming presidential election.</p>\r\n<p>Voting in the presidential election also has a significant impact on policies and <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\">government </a>leadership. The elected president will have the power to shape the direction of the country, including making decisions on issues such as healthcare, <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/education\">education</a>, immigration, and national security. By casting a vote, citizens can help determine who will lead the country and what policies will be implemented. Every vote counts, and each individual has the power to influence the outcome of the election.</p>\r\n<p>In conclusion, voting in the presidential election is a crucial aspect of democracy and has a significant impact on the direction of the country. By exercising their right to vote, citizens can actively participate in democracy and have a say in the policies and decisions that affect their lives. Therefore, it is important for every eligible citizen to take part in the upcoming presidential election and make their voice heard. Take part in the <strong>survey “Are you planning to vote in the next presidential election?“</strong> on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-05 17:19:17', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1685985557, NULL),
(447, 'Why are there so many wildfires in Canada?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Natural Causes such as Lightning Strikes</h3>\r\n<p>One of the natural causes of wildfires in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Canada\">Canada </a>is lightning strikes. According to Flannigan, a wildfire researcher, higher temperatures increase the likelihood of lightning, which can ignite fires. In addition, research suggests that heat and drought associated with climate change and global warming are contributing to the increase in the size and intensity of wildfires in Alberta, British Columbia, and Saskatchewan. The impact of climate change on wildfires is a growing concern and requires immediate action to mitigate its effects. It is important to address the root causes of wildfires to prevent future disasters and protect the environment.</p>\r\n<p>Human activity and negligence are also significant contributors to the prevalence of wildfires in Canada. A study shows that humans caused more than 1.2 million of the 1.5 million wildfires in the<a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\"> United States</a>. Campfires left unattended, debris caught in recreational vehicles\' undercarriages, and uncontrolled burning of agricultural lands are some of the human activities that can ignite wildfires. Human activity causes approximately 40% of wildfires. It is crucial to educate people on the importance of fire safety and taking necessary precautions to prevent wildfires.</p>\r\n<p>The increasing frequency and intensity of wildfires in Canada is a complex issue that requires a multifaceted approach to address. Climate change, natural causes, and human activity are all contributing factors. It is important to take steps to mitigate climate change, such as reducing greenhouse gas emissions, to prevent future wildfires. Additionally, it is essential to educate people on fire safety and take necessary precautions to prevent human-caused wildfires. You can also share your opinion on this topic by participating in the <strong>survey “Why are there so many wildfires in Canada?”</strong> on our website en.referendum.social and writing your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-06 15:28:44', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686065324, NULL),
(448, 'Do you think the destruction of the Dam in Nova Kakhovka will benefit Russia or not?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The potential impact of the destruction of the Dam in Nova Kakhovka</h3>\r\n<p>The destruction of the Dam in Nova Kakhovka has the potential to cause significant environmental damage to the surrounding ecosystem. The dam has been in place for decades, and its removal could result in the release of large amounts of sediment and pollutants into the Dnipro River and the Black Sea. This could negatively impact the region\'s wildlife and natural habitats, as well as the quality of the water supply for nearby communities. The long-term effects of this destruction on the environment are still uncertain, and it is essential to closely monitor the situation to mitigate any potential damage.</p>\r\n<p>The destruction of the Dam in Nova Kakhovka also has the potential to cause significant economic impacts on the region. The dam provides hydroelectric power and water to both <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine </a>and <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia</a>, and its destruction could disrupt the energy supply to both countries. The flooding caused by the destruction of the dam could also damage nearby crops and farmland, impacting the agricultural industry in the region. The economic fallout from this event could be significant and long-lasting, and it is important to consider the potential consequences carefully.</p>\r\n<p>The destruction of the Dam in Nova Kakhovka has sparked a debate about its potential benefits and drawbacks for Russia and Ukraine. To gather opinions on this topic, a survey has been launched on en.referendum.social. The survey asks participants whether they think the destruction of the dam will benefit Russia or not and invites them to share their thoughts on the matter in the comments. It is essential to consider the opinions of both sides and engage in constructive dialogue to find a solution that is beneficial for all parties involved.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-06 15:38:45', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686065925, NULL),
(449, 'How optimistic are you about the future of the planet about climate change?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Results of the Poll on&nbsp;How optimistic are you about the future of the planet about climate change?</h3>\r\n<p>A recent poll conducted on the website en.referendum.social asked respondents about their level of optimism towards the future of the planet in relation to climate change. The results showed that 45% of respondents were optimistic, 35% were pessimistic, and 20% were unsure. Interestingly, a separate poll conducted by PBS NewsHour and Generation Lab found that young people aged 13 to 29 were more optimistic about the future of the planet despite concerns about climate change. These results suggest that there is a mix of optimism and pessimism among the general population regarding the future of the planet in relation to climate change.</p>\r\n<p>The factors influencing optimism and pessimism towards climate change are complex and multifaceted. Some individuals are optimistic due to recent progress and increased attention towards environmental issues, such as the rise in environmental, social, and good governance priorities. Others are optimistic about the potential impact of policy and individual efforts to address climate change. On the other hand, some individuals may be pessimistic due to a lack of progress and perceived inadequate <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\">government </a>responses to climate change. Additionally, assessments of future environmental conditions and perceptions of how the world is changing can also influence optimism and pessimism towards climate change.</p>\r\n<p>The poll on en.referendum.social provides an opportunity for individuals to share their opinions and thoughts on the future of the planet in relation to climate change. By participating in the poll and leaving comments, individuals can contribute to a larger conversation about this important topic. While there may be a mix of optimism and pessimism towards climate change, it is important to continue discussing and working towards solutions to address this global issue. As one respondent noted, \"I am optimistic that \'The Age of Climate Change\' will end positively. I am hopeful that we will completely transition to clean and renewable [energy]\"</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-07 18:01:04', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686160864, NULL),
(450, 'Do you think Russia will blow up Zaporizhzhya NPP?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Analysis of the potential threat to Zaporizhzhya NPP</h3>\r\n<p>The Zaporizhzhya Nuclear Power Plant (NPP) has been a topic of concern due to its location in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Ukraine\">Ukraine</a>, which has been the site of ongoing conflict between Ukraine and <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Russia\">Russia</a>. The possibility of an attack on the NPP by Russia cannot be ruled out, especially given the recent breach of a dam in southern Ukraine, which has put further stress on the NPP. In addition, the human factor, such as chronic fatigue or stress, can also increase the risk of a nuclear accident. The political instability caused by the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/War\">war </a>and mounting casualties could also contribute to a potential threat to the NPP. These factors highlight the need for increased vigilance and preparedness to prevent any potential threats to the NPP.</p>\r\n<p>An attack on the Zaporizhzhya NPP could have severe consequences, both for Ukraine and the wider region. Shelling near the NPP could trigger a radiation leak, leading to widespread contamination and significant health risks. The demolition of the Kakhovka Hydroelectric Power Plant dam by Russians may also have negative consequences for the NPP. Furthermore, the disconnection of the NPP from its main power line due to Russian shelling in November 2022 highlights the vulnerability of the NPP to attacks. The consequences of such an attack could be catastrophic, and therefore, it is essential to take necessary measures to prevent any such incidents from occurring.</p>\r\n<p>The potential threat to the Zaporizhzhya NPP is a matter of concern for not only Ukraine but also the wider international community. It is important to gather opinions and perspectives on this issue to better understand the potential risks and develop effective strategies to mitigate them. Therefore, we invite you to take part in our <strong>survey “Do you think Russia will blow up Zaporizhzhya NPP?” </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and share your thoughts in the comments section. It is crucial to have an open and informed discussion on this topic to ensure the safety and security of the NPP and the people living in its vicinity.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-08 17:30:06', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686245406, NULL),
(451, 'Are you confident in the fairness of the US court system?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Factors that influence public perception of the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">US </a>court system\'s fairness</h3>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/media\">Media </a>coverage of high-profile cases can significantly influence public perception of the fairness of the US court system. The media often focuses on sensational cases, which can create a distorted perception of the legal system. This can lead to a lack of confidence in the court system, as people may believe that high-profile cases receive preferential treatment. Additionally, the media\'s portrayal of certain groups, such as minorities and low-income individuals, can contribute to negative perceptions of the legal system. For example, a 2015 survey found that nearly half of young Americans believe that the US justice system has racial and ethnic biases. Therefore, the media\'s coverage of the legal system can have a significant impact on public confidence in the fairness of the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/court\">court </a>system.</p>\r\n<p>Socioeconomic and racial disparities in the legal system can also contribute to negative perceptions of the fairness of the US court system. Studies have shown that minorities and low-income individuals are disproportionately affected by the legal system\'s biases, including racial profiling, harsher sentencing, and limited access to legal resources&nbsp;. These disparities can lead to a lack of trust in the legal system and a belief that the system is inherently unfair. Furthermore, the recent decline in confidence in the US Supreme Court, with only 25% of Americans expressing confidence in the court, suggests that there is a need for reform to address these disparities and improve public perception of the fairness of the court system.</p>\r\n<p>It is important to understand the factors that influence public perception of the fairness of the US court system. To gain a better understanding of public opinion on this topic, we invite you to participate in our survey <strong>“Are you confident in the fairness of the US court system?”</strong> on our website en.referendum.social. We encourage you to share your opinions and thoughts on this topic in the comments section. As American democracy faces a dangerous inflection point, it is essential to engage in dialogue and take action to address disparities and improve the fairness of the US court system</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-09 19:11:43', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686337903, NULL),
(452, 'Are you going to vote for Biden in the next presidential election?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Factors to consider when deciding whether or not to vote for Biden in the next <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">USA </a>presidential election</h3>\r\n<p>When deciding whether or not to vote for Biden in the next presidential election, it is important to consider his political experience and record. Biden has been involved in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Politics\">politics </a>for over 40 years, serving as a senator for Delaware and as Vice <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/president\">President </a>under Barack Obama. His experience in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\">government </a>and foreign policy may be an important factor for voters who prioritize stability and experience in their candidates. However, some voters may view his long tenure in politics as a negative and may prefer a fresh perspective from a newer candidate.</p>\r\n<p>Another factor to consider when deciding whether or not to vote for Biden is his policies compared to other candidates. Voters should research and compare the policies of each candidate to determine which aligns best with their own beliefs and values. Biden\'s policies include expanding access to healthcare, addressing climate change, and increasing taxes on the wealthy. It is important for voters to consider which policies are most important to them and which candidate\'s policies align with their priorities.</p>\r\n<p>Finally, it is important for voters to participate in the democratic process and exercise their right to vote. In the upcoming election, voters should research the candidates, their policies, and their records to make an informed decision. It is also important to participate in polls and surveys, such as the<strong> “Are you going to vote for Biden in the next presidential election?”</strong> on en.referendum.social, to understand the opinions and perspectives of others. Additionally, voters should make sure they are aware of their polling place and any necessary identification requirements. Ultimately, it is up to each individual to decide whether or not to vote for Biden, but it is important to make an informed decision and participate in the democratic process</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-12 17:30:28', '2023-06-12 17:30:38', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686591028, 1686591038),
(453, 'Do you agree that Trump should be put in jail?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Reasons for and against putting <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Trump\">Trump </a>in jail</h3>\r\n<p>The argument for putting former President Donald Trump in jail stems from allegations of criminal activities. The Justice Department has been investigating Trump for various charges, including obstruction of justice and incitement of insurrection. Some argue that Trump\'s actions on January 6, 2021, when a mob of his supporters stormed the Capitol building, warrant criminal charges. Additionally, a majority of Americans believe that an indictment stemming from one of the pending criminal probes of Trump should bar him from running for president again. Supporters of this argument believe that holding Trump accountable for his actions is necessary to uphold the rule of law and prevent future abuses of power.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, there are those who argue against putting Trump in jail. Some believe that prosecuting a former president would be deeply unsettling for the <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">USA </a>citizens. Others argue that it may be politically difficult for an indicted candidate, who could become a convicted criminal, to win votes. Furthermore, rank-and-file GOP voters seem largely undeterred by the multiple criminal investigations against Trump. A recent poll found that nearly two-thirds of Americans said that former President Trump should not be allowed to serve as president again, but far fewer, roughly a quarter, think Trump will actually be prosecuted. Those who oppose putting Trump in jail argue that the legal system should not be used as a political tool and that the focus should be on healing and moving forward as a nation.</p>\r\n<p>The decision of whether or not to put Trump in jail remains a controversial and divisive topic. It is important for individuals to educate themselves on the facts and make their own informed opinions. To further contribute to the discussion, individuals can take part in the <strong>survey “Do you agree that Trump should be put in jail?” </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and share their thoughts in the comments section. Ultimately, the decision of whether or not to prosecute Trump will be up to the Justice Department and the legal system.</p>\r\n<div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"mainEntity\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Question\">\r\n    <h2 itemprop=\"name\">Do you agree that Trump should be put in jail?</h2>\r\n    <div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\r\n        <div itemprop=\"text\">\r\n            According to our sociological research for theme \"Do you agree that Trump should be put in jail?\" there is 88% voted \"Yes\", and 12% voted \"No\". The survey was conducted all over the world. Data  of update as  September 18, 2023.\r\n            <br>\r\n            <p>You can also vote in this poll via the link <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/poll/453\"> Click here </a>.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>', 1186, 1, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-13 19:34:51', '2023-06-23 00:37:37', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686684891, 1687480657),
(454, 'Do you think that Turkey should be kicked out of the NATO?', '<div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"mainEntity\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Question\">\r\n    <h2 itemprop=\"name\">Do you think that Turkey should be kicked out of the NATO?</h2>\r\n    <div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\r\n        <div itemprop=\"text\">\r\n            According to our sociological research for theme \"Do you think that Turkey should be kicked out of the NATO?\" there is 60% voted \"Yes\", and 40% voted \"No\". The survey was conducted all over the world. Data of update as September 21, 2023.\r\n            <br>\r\n            <p>You can also vote in this poll via the link <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/poll/454\"> Click here </a>.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-14 17:17:02', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686763022, NULL),
(455, 'What do you think about the attacks on arts and museums as a kind of protest?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The impact of attacks on arts and museums as a form of protest</h3>\r\n<p>Attacks on arts and museums as a form of protest have a significant impact on the destruction of cultural heritage. Reports of the destruction and looting of art and objects of cultural heritage occur almost daily, at local, regional, national, and international levels. The intentional destruction of cultural heritage has a long history, with political, religious, and ideological motives behind many of these attacks. Such attacks not only result in the loss of irreplaceable cultural artifacts but also damage the collective memory of communities and societies. As a result, attacks on arts and museums as a form of protest can have a lasting negative impact on cultural heritage.</p>\r\n<p>There are alternative forms of peaceful protest that can be done by <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people </a>to express dissent and bring attention to social and issues in <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/nature\">nature </a>. Non-violent but disruptive forms of protest can gain attention and be effective in raising awareness of issues. Art can also be used as a form of social protest and has the potential to increase public awareness of important issues. However, attacks on arts and museums as a form of protest can be counterproductive, as they may alienate potential supporters and detract from the message being conveyed.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about the attacks on arts and museums as a kind of protest? Take part in the <strong>survey “What do you think about the attacks on arts and museums as a kind of protest?“ </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments. The debate surrounding attacks on arts and museums as a form of protest is ongoing, with some arguing that these attacks are an effective way to bring attention to important issues,while others argue that they are counterproductive and damaging.It is important to consider the potential consequences of such attacks and to explore alternative forms of peaceful protest.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-15 16:20:43', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686846043, NULL),
(456, 'Should the government provide free healthcare for all citizens?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Arguments for and against <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/government\">government </a>provided free healthcare</h3>\r\n<p>The idea of government-provided free healthcare has been a topic of debate for many years. Those in favor of free healthcare argue that it is a basic human right and that the government has a responsibility to ensure that all citizens have access to healthcare services. Free healthcare would eliminate the financial burden of medical care, making it more accessible to low-income individuals and families. Additionally, free healthcare would promote preventative care, which could ultimately lead to a healthier population and a reduction in healthcare costs in the long run.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, those against free healthcare argue that it would lead to inefficiencies in the healthcare system and could result in decreased quality of care. Critics argue that government-run healthcare systems are often bureaucratic and slow to respond to patient needs. There are also concerns about the cost of implementing such a system, as well as the potential for increased taxes to fund it. Furthermore, some <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people </a>may prefer to have the option of private healthcare and not be forced to participate in a government-run system.</p>\r\n<p>The debate over whether the government should provide free healthcare for all citizens is a complex issue with valid arguments on both sides. According to a recent poll, 57% of Americans believe that the government should ensure health coverage for all citizens, while 53% favor a health system based on private insurance. However, only about one in ten registered voters would support a Medicare for all system if it meant abolishing private health insurance. Ultimately, the decision of whether or not to implement free healthcare rests on the balance between the potential benefits and drawbacks of such a system. What do you think about this topic? Take part in the <strong>survey “Should the government provide free healthcare for all citizens?“ </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-16 18:28:59', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1686940139, NULL),
(457, 'Do you support the U.S. “One China” policy?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>The U.S. \"One China\" policy and its implications</h3>\r\n<p>The <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/USA\">USA </a>\"One <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/China\">China</a>\" policy is a diplomatic policy that has been in place since 1979. It acknowledges the People\'s Republic of China (PRC) as the sole legitimate government of China and recognizes that <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/Taiwan\">Taiwan </a>is a part of China. The policy is guided by the Taiwan Relations Act and the three Joint Communiques. However, the policy remains somewhat ambiguous and subject to different interpretations. Beijing asserts that there is only \"one China\" and views the PRC as the only legitimate government of China. The policy has been a contentious issue in U.S.-China relations and has implications for regional stability and security.</p>\r\n<p>There are arguments for supporting the U.S. \"One China\" policy. Some argue that the policy provides stability in the region and prevents conflict between the U.S. and China. Others argue that the policy is necessary for economic and trade relations between the U.S. and China. However, there are also arguments against the policy, with some arguing that it undermines Taiwan\'s sovereignty and ability to participate in international organizations. The debate over the policy remains ongoing and has implications for U.S. foreign policy in the Asia-Pacific region.</p>\r\n<p>What do you think about the U.S. \"One China\" policy? Share your opinion by taking part in the survey<strong> \"Do you support the U.S. \'One China\' policy\" </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and leave your comments. As a contentious issue in U.S.-China relations, it is important to understand the perspectives and opinions of the public on this topic.</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-19 17:44:42', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1687196682, NULL),
(458, 'Do you agree that zoos should be banned?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html --><h3>Arguments for and against banning zoos</h3>\r\n<p>There are strong arguments for banning zoos, particularly regarding ethical concerns regarding animal welfare. Many animal rights activists argue that zoos are prisons for animals and that keeping them captive is cruel and unnecessary. They also argue that zoos do not educate the public enough to justify keeping animals in captivity. Furthermore, there are concerns about the unnatural habitats in which animals are kept and the killing or selling of surplus animals. While zoo advocates and conservationists argue that zoos save endangered species and educate the public, many animal rights activists believe the cost of animal suffering outweighs these benefits. Should zoos be banned? It is a complex issue that requires careful consideration of the arguments for and against.</p>\r\n<p>On the other hand, some argue that zoos are necessary for conservation efforts and that they play an important role in educating <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people&nbsp;</a>about endangered species. They believe that zoos provide a unique opportunity for people to see animals up close and learn about them in a way that they wouldn\'t be able to in the wild. Additionally, some argue that zoos provide a safe haven for animals that have been injured or orphaned and would not be able to survive in the wild. However, many of these arguments have been challenged by animal rights activists who argue that there are better ways to conserve and educate about endangered species without keeping them in captivity.</p>\r\n<p>Ultimately, the debate over whether zoos should be banned is a complex one that requires careful consideration of the arguments for and against. It is important to consider the ethical concerns regarding animal welfare and whether the benefits of zoos outweigh the costs of animal suffering. What do you think about this topic? Take part in the <strong>survey “Do you agree that zoos should be banned?” </strong>on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments</p>', 1186, 0, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-20 17:37:51', '2024-05-19 21:16:54', 0, 1186, 1186, 1687282671, NULL),
(459, 'Do you think that Titanic missing sub will be found?', '<!-- x-tinymce/html -->\r\n<h3>Possibilities and factors affecting the discovery of Titanic\'s missing sub</h3>\r\n<p>The possibility of discovering the Titanic\'s missing sub has increased due to technological advances in underwater exploration. According to oceanographer David Wright, modern technology has made it possible to explore any part of the ocean, including the deepest parts of the Mariana Trench. This means that the search for the missing submersible can leverage the latest technology to explore the ocean floor in greater detail, increasing the chances of finding the sub.</p>\r\n<p>However, the size and depth of the ocean present significant challenges in the search for the missing sub. The Titanic wreckage is located at a depth of approximately 12,500 feet, which is twice as deep as the Grand Canyon. This depth, combined with the vast size of the ocean, makes the search for the missing sub a daunting task. Despite this, rescue crews have reported hearing banging sounds during the search, indicating the possibility of survived <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/tag/people\">people</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Do you think that Titanic\'s missing sub will be found? Share your opinion by taking part in the <strong>survey “Do you think that Titanic missing sub will be found?“</strong> on our website en.referendum.social and also write your opinion in the comments. The outcome of the search for the missing sub remains uncertain, but with the latest technology and the determination of rescue crews, there is hope that the sub will be found and any survivors rescued</p>\r\n<div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"mainEntity\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Question\">\r\n    <h2 itemprop=\"name\">Do you think that Titanic missing sub will be found?</h2>\r\n    <div itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"acceptedAnswer\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\r\n        <div itemprop=\"text\">\r\n            According to our sociological research for them \"Do you think that Titanic missing sub will be found?\" there is 71% voted \"Yes\", and 29% voted \"No\". The survey was conducted all over the world. Data of update as September 14, 2023.\r\n            <br>\r\n            <p>You can also vote in this poll via the link <a href=\"https://en.referendum.social/poll/459\"> Click here </a>.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>', 1186, 1, 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '2023-06-21 17:14:16', '2023-06-23 18:14:58', 0, 1186, 1186, 1687367656, 1687544098);
